      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(text): bound compactText for tiny caps",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- make `compactText(value, maxLength)` obey its maximum length for caps smaller than the three-character ellipsis\n- add focused boundary regression coverage for caps 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 16, and 17\n- narrow the original mixed helper patch to the independently reproducible issue\n\n## Proof\n\nBuilt output on Node 26.5.0:\n\n```text\ncap  output                 length\n0    \"\"                     0\n1    \"a\"                    1\n2    \"ab\"                   2\n3    \"...\"                  3\n4    \"a...\"                 4\n16   \"abcdefghijklm...\"     16\n17   \"abcdef ... uvwxyz\"    17\n```\n\n- focused regression: 1 passed, 0 failed\n- AutoReview: clean, no accepted or actionable findings\n- local full check reached 1,353 passing tests; four unchanged environment-sensitive failures reproduce outside this diff because this macOS host lacks GNU `timeout` and the runtime packaging test does not resolve the compiler service under this local setup\n- hosted exact-head CI is the merge gate\n\nThanks @anagnorisis2peripeteia for the report, original fix, and boundary tests.\n\nCloses #573.\n",
